# Database — {{ project_name }}

This project uses **MongoDB** as its database driver.

MongoDB stores data in **collections** (not SQL tables), so there are no SQL
migration files in this project.  Schema shape is enforced at the application
layer via your model definitions.

## Suggested tools

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `pymongo` | Low-level driver (already in your dependencies) |
| [MongoEngine](https://mongoengine.org) | Document-Object Mapper (similar to an ORM) |
| [Beanie](https://beanie-odm.dev) | Async ODM built on Motor + Pydantic |

## Schema validation (optional)

MongoDB supports server-side JSON Schema validation on collections.  Example:

```python
from pymongo import MongoClient

client = MongoClient(MONGO_URI)
db = client["{{ pkg_name }}"]

db.create_collection(
    "users",
    validator={
        "$jsonSchema": {
            "bsonType": "object",
            "required": ["name", "email"],
            "properties": {
                "name":  {"bsonType": "string"},
                "email": {"bsonType": "string"},
            },
        }
    },
)
```

## Indexes

Create indexes at startup (idempotent — safe to re-run):

```python
db["users"].create_index("email", unique=True)
```
